      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I will clarify for Naqtn, in case his language is difficult to understand. \n\nWhat I believe he is saying, is that Repeat should not be tied to Reset On Enable. Repeat means it fires after every time interval. Reset On Enable means that OnEnable, the timer starts from 0 and does the action once, even if it had already been done once in the instance. If the object is disabled and the-enabled, without Repeat on, it should act as a “fresh” timer. It should NOT require Repeat to work.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
