  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-04-06T02:32:59.215Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "(Though I already posted to discord open-beta-discussion, I report here again for not forgotten.)\n\nI tested OnTimer trigger issues I reported before with build 741. I think this fix is done in incomplete way. As release notes said, my example is \"not set to Repeat\". But I think this setup must be reusable even if \"not set to Repeat\".\nI guess the maintainer thought: \"non Repeat\" means \"it is one-shot timer\" so it fires no more than once. But this setup use \"Reset On Enable\". OnTimer document says \"Reset On Enable\" means \"If true the timer will be reset\". IMO, this \"reset\" should include resetting a state of \"it already fired (or not) as one-shot timer\". (And then, it will be reusable.)\nIf current fix is correct, OnTimer document should explain different meaning of \"reset\" in \"Repeat\" and \"Reset On Enable\" parameters. I think that will be a source of confusion.\n\n(original report: https://vrchat.canny.io/bug-reports/p/ontimer-reset-on-enable-does-not-reset-its-started-time )",
